#
# Scoped ignore-file for .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile (issue #86).
#
# The repo-root .dockerignore is "* / !Dockerfile / !dist/*.whl": it keeps the
# MAIN container build context tiny (that Dockerfile only COPYs the version-
# matched wheel). But ClusterFuzzLite builds .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile with
# the repo ROOT as context, and that Dockerfile needs the full source tree
# (COPY . $SRC/qureddy) plus .clusterfuzzlite/build.sh. Under the root ignore
# those are all excluded, so `COPY .clusterfuzzlite/build.sh` and `COPY .` fail.
#
# BuildKit uses a "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" file, when present, INSTEAD
# of the root .dockerignore for that specific build. This file therefore gives
# the fuzz build the full context it needs while leaving the root .dockerignore
# (and the main container build) untouched. Excludes only never-needed noise.
.git
.venv
dist
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
